    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "df6be6ca_48423615",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/VpnManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 78,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-06T13:58:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understand this will also stop a VPN started with VpnService, but do we intend to later expand the surface of VpnManager to also manage other aspects of non-platform VPNs ? If not, this will stick out as an inconsistency.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 78,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 78,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "0b862988e44d8d70e155d9a70e677995f49d596e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4edab9f5_342fa678",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/VpnManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 78,
      "author": {
        "id": 1221725
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-07T00:07:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Long term, yes. While there\u0027s not much I can do about the VpnService API, I would like this class to be the primary API surface for any new VPN APIs.\n\nAlso, in the VpnService API, there\u0027s no way for a VPN to \"stop\" itself - it relies on the TUN FD dying (and the kernel cleaning up the TUN interface). This seemed like a consistent way to allow an app to directly tell the system that it wants to shut down, regardless of what type of VPN they\u0027re running.\n\nThoughts?\n\nI also don\u0027t mind making this profile specific, but that seemed like an artificial limitation for nothing really gained.",
      "parentUuid": "df6be6ca_48423615",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 78,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 78,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "0b862988e44d8d70e155d9a70e677995f49d596e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aaaff96e_40bb554d",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/VpnManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 78,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-08T00:54:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So generally I think it would be good as a design when VpnManager handles managing all styles of VPN, but it sounds like the surface we have here is all we\u0027ll have for R, and possibly for S too. And at that point I do think the API looks nicer if this is just stopProvisionedVpnProfile.\n\nWhen VpnManager has methods to manage other kinds of VPN, we may want to add a stopVpn() call that stops everything (and possibly symmetrical calls figuring out for the app what it wants if that makes sense at that time).\n\nSo I think we should make this stopProvisionedVpnProfile, and have it refuse to run if the running VPN is not a platform VPN.",
      "parentUuid": "4edab9f5_342fa678",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 78,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 78,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "0b862988e44d8d70e155d9a70e677995f49d596e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
